sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-kriegman-xenobot-evolutionary-biobots> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kriegman-xenobot-evolutionary-biobots-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kriegman-xenobot-evolutionary-biobots-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Kriegman et al. (2020, 2021) Xenobot evolutionary biomechanics & kinematic self-replication — MorphoEval overall 91.3/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 post-remediation evaluation of `2020-kriegman-xenobot-evolutionary-biobots.py` (91.5/100, up from 59.5/100 in Pass 1; +32.0 overall). The remediated script couples passive animal-cap ectoderm ($\\Delta V = 0$) and rhythmic contractile cardiac progenitor ($f_{\\mathrm{act}} = 1.5\\text{ Hz}, \\varepsilon_0 = 0.18$) voxel spring-lattice mechanics with the AFPO phase-randomization transferability filter, reproducing all 5 Kriegman et al. (2020, 2021) experimental regimes: evolved ventral-concavity bipedal walking ($1.95\\ L_{\\mathrm{body}}$), phase-randomized cardiomyocyte noise retention ($74.3\\%$ vs $13.3\\%$ for checkerboard), $180^\\circ$ dorsal inversion collapse ($0.12\\ L_{\\mathrm{body}}$), $50\\%$ mechanical laceration wound-closure recovery ($85.2\\%$), and $C$-shaped (\"Pac-Man\", $\\theta_{\\mathrm{mouth}} = 65^\\circ$) kinematic self-replication ($3$ daughter generations, $2.95\\times$ spherical yield), alongside automated convex-hull concavity ($0.1588$) and red-fluorescent cardiac core ($0.3647$) segmentation on `xenopus_biobot_specimen.jpg`, backed by 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_083_xenobot_evolutionary_biobots.lean`. Overall 91.3/100 (faithfulness 91.2, reproducibility 91.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 93, Morphological realism / specimen match 90, Parameter expressivity 91, Morphometric validation 91, Source and data traceability 93, Code-to-model traceability 91, Reproducibility package 91. Output judged: docs/media/xenobot_evolutionary_biobots_comparison.png: rendered output of 2020-kriegman-xenobot-evolutionary-biobots.py at 317bc3c, image/png, 795896 B, 2268×1863 px, artifact_sha256 3ada48180881707f50f622d45cf504c320a18eb4da0b54cbdabe1e669d3b119a (sha256 3ada48180881707f50f622d45cf504c320a18eb4da0b54cbdabe1e669d3b119a), spec_fingerprint 9611ac5308e60d5b8cd28bafdf0fb556acb91a73e85f822739154d38d1283ee9. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 9611ac5308e60d5b8cd28bafdf0fb556acb91a73e85f822739154d38d1283ee9; artifact_sha256: 3ada48180881707f50f622d45cf504c320a18eb4da0b54cbdabe1e669d3b119a; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/xenobot_evolutionary_biobots/paper_citations.bib=4f92785fb031ce11..., datasets/xenobot_evolutionary_biobots/scout_manifest.json=abbd461fb51acbc9..., datasets/xenobot_evolutionary_biobots/xenobot_evolutionary_biobots_reference.json=256b3387af983583..., datasets/xenobot_evolutionary_biobots/xenopus_biobot_specimen.jpg=13e063704f07254f...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-xenobot-evolutionary-biobots-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Kriegman, Blackiston, Levin & Bongard (2020) PNAS 117:1853-1859 voxel-based passive ectoderm + contractile cardiac progenitor spring-lattice design pipeline, AFPO phase-randomization transferability filter, dorsal inversion locomotion collapse, and mechanical laceration regeneration | Kriegman, Blackiston, Levin & Bongard (2021) PNAS 118:e2112672118 C-shaped ('Pac-Man') kinematic self-replication sweeping dissociated Xenopus stem cells into multi-generational daughter spheroids; reconstructed_in_script: 2D sagittal 8x5 voxel spring-lattice locomotion simulator across 5 experimental regimes, 60-generation AFPO pareto evolution, and 2D arena kinematic stem-cell compaction across mouth angles theta_mouth in [0, 120] deg | Automated chromatic R-B/R-G segmentation and 2D convex-hull solidity/concavity analysis on xenopus_biobot_specimen.jpg (concavity = 0.1588, cardiac fraction = 0.3647, ectoderm fraction = 0.6353); transfer_boundary: Reduced 2D sagittal voxel spring-lattice and orbital stem-cell sweeping kinematics calibrated to 3D VoxCAD and wet-lab Xenopus laevis biobot trajectories; does_not_claim: Full 3D fluid-structure Stokes ciliary boundary-element hydrodynamics or single-cell transcriptomic reprogramming after laceration." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple mucociliary boundary-layer Stokes flow around the C-shaped Pac-Man concavity to hydrodynamic stem-cell capture.",
            "remediation needed: Extend the 2D sagittal 8x5 voxel lattice to a full 8x8x7 3D VoxCAD finite-element mesh with explicit fluid drag." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.913"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (primary) + Claude Sonnet 5.5 High (independent second assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://deepmind.google> .
}

